 Round Mirror</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#6-flank-the-mirror-with-two-sconces">6. Flank the Mirror With Two Sconces</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#7-choose-warm-dimmable-light">7. Choose Warm, Dimmable Light</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#sink-storage-and-smallspace-ideas">Sink, Storage and Small-Space Ideas</a><ul class="kb-table-of-contents-list-sub"><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#8-style-under-a-pedestal-sink">8. Style Under a Pedestal Sink</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#9-pick-a-floating-vanity">9. Pick a Floating Vanity</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#10-add-a-slim-shelf-above-the-sink">10. Add a Slim Shelf Above the Sink</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#11-decorate-the-wall-above-the-toilet">11. Decorate the Wall Above the Toilet</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#finishing-touches-guests-notice">Finishing Touches Guests Notice</a><ul class="kb-table-of-contents-list-sub"><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#12-set-up-a-guest-towel-station">12. Set Up a Guest Towel Station</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#13-add-one-easy-plant">13. Add One Easy Plant</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#14-use-scent-safely">14. Use Scent Safely</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#15-lay-a-small-washable-rug">15. Lay a Small Washable Rug</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#16-stick-to-one-metal-finish">16. Stick to One Metal Finish</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#before-and-after-putting-the-ideas-together">Before and After: Putting the Ideas Together</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#common-powder-room-decor-mistakes">Common Powder Room Decor Mistakes</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#powder-room-decor-faq">Powder Room Decor FAQ</a><ul class="kb-table-of-contents-list-sub"><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#what-is-the-difference-between-a-powder-room-and-a-half-bath">What is the difference between a powder room and a half bath?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-do-i-make-a-small-powder-room-look-bigger">How do I make a small powder room look bigger?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#can-you-put-wallpaper-in-a-powder-room">Can you put wallpaper in a powder room?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#what-color-is-best-for-a-powder-room">What color is best for a powder room?</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#final-thoughts">Final Thoughts</a></li></ul></div></nav>


<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What Makes a Powder Room Different?</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A powder room is built for short visits: wash your hands, check the mirror, leave. Because there is no tub or shower, humidity stays much lower than in a full bathroom, so materials such as paper wallpaper, framed prints and linen towels are a safer bet here. The sink still splashes, though, so choose wipeable paint and keep paper and fabric a little away from the faucet.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The other difference is size. Many half baths are barely wider than a closet, so decor has to work around the fixtures, not in front of them. The National Kitchen and Bath Association (NKBA) guidelines, as summarized in Bob Vila&#8217;s <a href="https://www.bobvila.com/articles/15445-the-basics-of-bathroom-design/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">guide to bathroom design measurements</a>, recommend at least 18 inches of elbow room between a toilet and a vanity or another fixture (codes allow 15 inches) and 30 inches between the front edge of the toilet or vanity and any other fixture or wall, where codes allow 21. The same guide recommends 20 inches from the center of the sink to the side wall (code minimum 15) and puts the toilet paper holder about 26 inches above the floor and 8 to 12 inches in front of the bowl.</p>



